              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "કેદી — kedī — \"a prisoner; a captive\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "જો પોલીસ સમયસર પહોંચી ગઈ તો કેદી બચી જશે. jo polīs samaysar pahõcī gaī to kedī bacī jaśe. If the police get there in time, the captive will be saved."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A masculine or feminine noun, by the person meant."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "કેદી (kedī) is usually traced to Persian qaidī, \"a prisoner\", from qaid, captivity, a word Persian took from Arabic. It is used of a man or a woman."
            }
          ]
        },
